1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Higguf#7 — built from random initialization.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The current milestone is an exact 2.064-billion-parameter decoder-only text model.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:21,000
It is not based on a pretrained model or an API.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Two free NVIDIA T4 GPUs on Kaggle ran fully sharded training with CPU offload.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
That completed six small pilot updates on an approved WikiText-2 stream.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The logged loss moved from 1572.75 on update one to 1189.44 on update six.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:57,000
This proves the distributed training path works. It does not mean the model is fully trained.

8
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:06,000
There is no public checkpoint in this release, and image and file generation are future work.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Next: lawful corpus preparation, much more training, evaluation, and an 18B architecture roadmap.
